      "annotations": {
        "change_summary": "Replaced the initial-level-set passthrough with sketch translation search, exact post-reinitialization objective modeling, and bounded boundary refinement using observed labels.",
        "parent_sha256": null,
        "rationale": "The measured parent scored 293.22 by returning the weak initial field. The public sketch contains 485 interior cells and is translation-invariant under the published Procrustes loss, while the drillhole labels are displaced from the raw sketch. I now search feasible integer translations using skfmm distance and the published logistic/contact terms, retain several translation hypotheses because raster boundary edits are nonconvex, and perform a bounded one-cell boundary refinement near finite observations. The local objective reproduces the official Fortran-order sketch pairing and applies it after distance reinitialization. Public selfcheck passes; local official-objective score is 3.95 (loss_sketch 0.144, drillhole 3.81), versus parent 293.22."
      }
    },
    {
