        "positive_voxels": 484.0,
        "research_utility": -3.7968566397997594
      },
      "annotations": {
        "change_summary": "Added bounded two-pixel boundary moves after translation and one-pixel refinement to escape rasterization local minima while preserving the exact post-distance objective.",
        "parent_sha256": "5c0dc65e2b2fa67f1bae4f529b421759414cd33bd0c22f712914bca60cac14fa",
        "rationale": "The prior measured candidate reached loss 3.9505 but its one-cell coordinate descent was locally trapped. Exhaustive local experiments on the public fixture showed improving paired boundary toggles, reaching 3.7969 after four bounded pair iterations. This change retains the prior translation and exact Fortran-order Procrustes modeling, then searches at most 130 nearby boundary cells in pairs for four iterations under the wall-time bound. The 3-D/no-sketch path remains conservative and input-driven. Public selfcheck passes; local official score is loss_drillhole 3.7106 plus loss_sketch 0.0862, total 3.7969."
      }
    },
