      "annotations": {
        "change_summary": "Added physical-coordinate small-angle sketch rotations to the translation hypotheses and expanded bounded pair refinement, improving raster boundary alignment with measured labels.",
        "parent_sha256": "8fd8937866681d6929eb4efd037ebe90685dcaf683d6f0931b3e4805caf07270",
        "rationale": "The prior measured candidate reached 3.7969 using translation plus four pair moves. Public-data experiments showed a small rigid rotation of the sketch produced a better initial geometry because the drillhole cuts the body at a sloped raster boundary; eight pair-refinement passes then reached local loss 3.7338. The solver now searches six small physical-coordinate rotations in addition to translations, keeps the best hypotheses, and performs bounded pair moves under the time limit. It remains input-driven, preserves the conservative no-sketch/3D path, and public selfcheck passes. Local official components are drillhole 3.6934 and sketch 0.0404."
      }
